  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 222 of the laws of 2015 amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law, the general municipal law and the public officers law relating to\nowner liability for failure of an operator to comply with traffic-control\nindications in the city of White Plains, in relation to extending the\nprovisions of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S9237",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9237-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §15, Chap 222 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9237\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 222 of the laws of 2015 amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law, the general municipal law and the public officers law\nrelating to owner liability for failure of an operator to comply with\ntraffic-control indications in the city of White Plains, in relation to\nextending the provisions of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo extend the expiration date of the White Plains red light camera\nprogram\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill provides that sections three, nine, twelve-c,\nthirteen, and fourteen of section 15 of chapter 222 of the laws of 2015\nshall be deemed repealed December 1, 2029.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the sunset for the 2015 bill authorizing the City of\nWhite Plains to install and operate traffic-control signal photo viola-\ntion-monitoring devices or \"red light cameras,\" until December 1, 2029.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
